    "body": "### Description\nSince 759bd434 (\"feat(roslyn_ls): load solution/projects via --autoLoadProjects\"), opening any C# buffer prints:\n\n```\nroslyn_ls: minimum required version is 5.8.0; projects won't be loaded\n```\n\neven with a current `roslyn-language-server` (5.12.0-1.26426.8). Projects are in fact loaded properly (`--autoLoadProjects` works; the LSP log shows the project system running), so this is a false negative.\n\n### Cause\n`supports_autoload()` runs `{ bin, \"--version\" }`, but `roslyn-language-server` requires one of `--stdio` / `--pipe` even when only asking for the version:\n\n```\n$ roslyn-language-server --version\nExpected either --stdio or --pipe <name>.        # exit 4, stdout empty\n\n$ roslyn-language-server --stdio --version\n5.12.0-1.26426.8+3aeb96c9ecc56a5ee483558f9e648e33e7bfe756   # exit 0\n```\n\nSo `out.code == 0` is never true and the check always fails.\n\n### Environment\n- NVIM v0.12.6\n- nvim-lspconfig 460bb34e (contains 759bd434)\n- roslyn-language-server 5.12.0-1.26426.8 (Mason package `roslyn-language-server`, nuget.org)\n- .NET SDK 10.0.114 / Microsoft.NETCore.App 10.0.14\n\n### Suggested fix\nProbe with `--stdio --version`:\n\n```diff\n-  local out = vim.system({ bin, '--version' }, { text = true }):wait()\n+  local out = vim.system({ bin, '--stdio', '--version' }, { text = true }):wait()\n```\n\nOptionally, only warn when a version was successfully parsed and is actually < 5.8.0, instead of treating \"probe failed\" as \"too old\", so future CLI changes don't produce false errors.\n",
    "closed_at": "2026-11-02T13:18:35Z",
